Ability: s Charts

  Out of the several options for control charts, the s chart is excellent for being highly accurate and precise.

  These charts are generally very solid choices, but are unsuitable if you are only taking a single measurement.
  For example, if you were measuring website response times but only got one measurement per day, the s chart
  would not work as you need _at least_ 2 but preferably more like 5. If you do only have one measurement you
  should consider the I-MR chart instead.


  Background:
    Given the measurements have a precision of "0.001"
    And the value of k for k-sigma is "3"

