  Example: s chart constants
  SPC uses 4 constants (A₃, B₃, B₄, c₄) when calculating the LCLs and UCLs for X-Bar and S Charts.
  The value of c₄ depends solely on the sample size, n.
  The values of A₃, B₃, and B₄ depend on n and the sigma multiplier, k.
  The table below lists these constants for standard 3-sigma limits (k=3).

    Given a sample size of "<n>"
    Then the value of "c₄" constant is "<c₄>"
    Then the value of "A₃" factor is "<A₃>"
    Then the value of "B₃" factor is "<B₃>"
    Then the value of "B₄" factor is "<B₄>"

